      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.28,
      "end_seconds": 324.38,
      "duration_seconds": 31.1,
      "text": "having listened and examined, I think we're dealing with community-acquired pneumonia at this stage another possibility is acute bronchitis let's get a chest X-ray, for possible pneumonia it's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture i'm sending you for blood tests cos of pneumonia it's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture we'll begin with amoxicillin, 500 milligrams, three times a day, five days it's for chest infection"
